          205
        ]
      },
      "rawText": "Basic Ranged Attacks\nPrerequisites: Level 20, one of Firestarter, Fountain, \nFreezer, Guster, Materializer, or Zapper\nCost: 1 Tutor Point\nEffect: Choose one of the Capabilities listed in the \nprerequisites for this Poké Edge. Struggle Attacks \nmodified by that Capability may now be made at a range \nof up to 6 meters. This Poké Edge may be taken multiple \ntimes, selecting a different Capability each time."
    },
    "september": {
      "id": "sep-basic-ranged-level-directive",
      "collection": "generalContexts",
      "jsonSha256": "16a7ec1fdc2492493c260de4319bba349b776905e8872915c1072c15098db34c",
      "rawSha256": "7c04b57535cddecff338beae990d7679b27cee6415a33158cdc57190c7e7202e",
      "source": {
        "authorityId": "r04-s03",
        "status": "optional-playtest",
        "publicationDate": "2015-09",
        "datePrecision": "month",
        "path": "Core System/1.05 Errata/PTU September 2015 Playtest Packet.pdf",
        "sha256": "846c23a90f26d7deb7a86117622378bc60dc7c729a9a6b1e747ea67d4a1c6caf",
        "pdfPages": [
          9
        ]
      },
      "rawText": "Poké Edge Changes\nBasic\tRanged\tAttacks\tnow has no Level Prerequisite. "
    },
    "framework": {
      "id": "poke-edge-framework",
      "collection": "generalContexts",
      "jsonSha256": "4ec5c9a740f506d97ed70482ec0e3a56e3857bd183447cfc502b1568e61f283b",
      "rawSha256": "2f6f5529b660ecac2b41d82acf02a90fb66e422a90fa061141dfaa82742cd0a5",
      "source": {
        "authorityId": "r04-s12",
        "status": "standard-baseline",
        "publicationDate": null,
        "datePrecision": "unknown",
        "path": "Core System/Pokemon Tabletop United 1.05 Core.pdf",
        "sha256": "e5e0371031601c3ad0a04056771c17599a2d8826e5a5102ccd37f9b368108907",
        "pdfPages": [
          204
        ]
      },
      "rawText": "Poké Edges\nWhile many Features allow Tutor Points to be spent to improve your Pokémon, that does not mean Tutor Points \nneed to sit idly if you don’t have access to those Features.\nAfter an hour of training, Pokémon may spend Tutor Points to gain any of the Poké Edges listed below, provided \nthey meet all prerequisites. If a Pokémon ever loses prerequisites for a Poké Edge they have, it is removed and the \nTutor Points refunded.\nStat and Skill Poké Edges\nPokémon do not need to be limited by their natural \ninclinations. Trainers can use these Poké Edges to allow \ntheir Pokémon to excel in unexpected ways. "
    }
  },
